        {
            "heading": "Religious",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The Great Tribal Pillar is a special building that may only be built in the capital via targeted decision. Sponsor must be unreformed pagan , at least Duke-tier and independent."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Only one Great Pillar per realm."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Each Great Pillar increases the religion’s Moral Authority and provides some special bonuses to the province based on the religion."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "After a successfull siege or raid, the occupier can simply destroy the Great Pillar. This results in not only the loss of the granted 5% moral authority, but also in a temporary malus on troop morale for all pagans!"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "An infidel ruler can take decision to simply burn it down."
                },
